  "id": "pws",
  "term": "PWS",
  "definition": "PWS is a genetic condition seen in about 1 in 15,000 to 20,000 births, most often linked to changes involving chromosome 15. In psychology and development, it is associated with cognitive difficulties, especially in spatial abilities, attention, working memory, and executive functioning, which can interfere with school performance.",
